  <static seed="1755" source="Contrib/PCC/BasicAlgebra/SignedNumbersArithemtic/MultiplyWithNegativeIntegers20.pg">
    <statement><p>Multiply the following.
<ol label="a.">
<li>
<p><m>(-3)\cdot(-4)\cdot(-4)</m></p>
<p><fillin characters="8" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>7\cdot(-9)\cdot(-3)</m></p>
<p><fillin characters="8" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>(-91)\cdot(-66)\cdot0</m></p>
<p><fillin characters="8" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-48</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>189</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>a.</p>
<p><m>\begin{aligned}[t]
        (-3)\cdot(-4)\cdot(-4) \amp  = 12\cdot(-4) \\
                                     \amp  = {-48}
       \end{aligned}</m></p>
<p>b.</p>
<p><m>\begin{aligned}[t]
         7\cdot(-9)\cdot(-3) \amp  = -63\cdot(-3)  \\
                       \amp  = {189}  
       \end{aligned}</m></p>
<p>c.</p>
<p><m>-91\cdot(-66)\cdot0 =0</m></p>
<p>Note that in the last case there is no need to waste time multiplying the first two numbers because any number multiplied by <m>0</m> equals <m>0</m>.</p>
</solution>
